      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:00Z",
      "text": "A truck bomb explodes near a military base in Planadas, Tolima Department, Colombia, killing four people, including a baby, and wounding several others.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-02:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:09Z",
      "text": "The Colombian conflict began on May 27, 1964, and is a low-intensity asymmetric war between the government of Colombia, paramilitary groups, crime syndicates,…",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383891635:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:17Z",
      "text": "On the map: Tolima Department, Colombia, where the reports place it.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-02:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The article lists two sides: Colombian cartels and paramilitaries:, La Oficina (1993–), Clan del Golfo (AGC) (2001–); Colombian rebel guerrilla groups:, FARC dissidents (2016–), CGSB (1987–1990).",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383891635:side-1",
        "wiki:box:1383891635:side-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:37Z",
      "text": "Casualties, as Wikipedia records them from its sources: on one side, 4,908 killed since 2004; 20,001 injured since 2004; on the other, 2,200 killed; 35,000 demobilized; 222 killed; 18,506 captured; 2,100 killed.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383891635:casualties-side-1-",
        "wiki:box:1383891635:casualties-side-2-"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:48Z",
